<section class="case-section">

  <div class="case-copy">

    <span class="section-kicker gold">
      Architecture Layers
    </span>


    <h2>
      Separate experience, orchestration and system ownership.
    </h2>


    <p>
      Each layer has a different responsibility.
      Keeping those responsibilities explicit
      reduces coupling and makes future change easier to reason about.
    </p>

  </div>



  <div class="case-layout">


    <article class="featured-case">

      <span class="case-status">
        Layer 01
      </span>


      <h3>
        Colleague & Customer Experience
      </h3>


      <p>
        Owns the interaction,
        case context,
        customer-facing guidance,
        work state
        and next operational action.
      </p>


      <div class="flow dark-flow">

        <span>
          Customer Intent
        </span>

        <span>
          Banker
        </span>

        <span>
          Case
        </span>

        <span>
          Tasks
        </span>

        <span>
          Outcome
        </span>

      </div>

    </article>



    <div class="roadmap">


      <details open>

        <summary>
          Layer 02 · Integration & Orchestration
        </summary>

        <p>
          Flowgear coordinates service calls,
          information transformation,
          routing,
          sequencing,
          error handling
          and integration monitoring.
        </p>

      </details>



      <details>

        <summary>
          Layer 03 · Enterprise Services
        </summary>

        <p>
          Reusable services expose
          eligibility,
          compliance,
          document,
          credit
          and fulfilment capabilities
          without forcing consumers
          to understand underlying implementation details.
        </p>

      </details>



      <details>

        <summary>
          Layer 04 · Systems of Record
        </summary>

        <p>
          Customer,
          product,
          credit,
          document,
          account
          and servicing systems
          retain ownership of authoritative business information.
        </p>

      </details>


    </div>

  </div>

</section>



